# 1. Introduction

The HoloJARVIS REST API allows external applications to communicate with the HoloJARVIS system.

Supported clients include:

- Desktop Application
- Web Dashboard
- Mobile Application
- Third-Party Integrations
- Future Plugins

All communication is JSON based.

---

# 2. Base URL

Development

```

http://localhost:8000/api/v1

```

Local Network

```

http://192.168.x.x:8000/api/v1

```

Production

```

https://your-domain.com/api/v1

```

---

# 3. Authentication

Protected endpoints require authentication.

Example Header

```http
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY
Content-Type: application/json
```

Future versions may support:

- JWT
- OAuth 2.0
- Multi-user Accounts

---

# 4. Response Format

Successful Response

```json
{
    "success": true,
    "message": "Command executed successfully",
    "data": {}
}
```

Error Response

```json
{
    "success": false,
    "error": "Invalid request"
}
```

---

# 5. Error Responses

| Status | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| 200 | Success |
| 201 | Created |
| 400 | Bad Request |
| 401 | Unauthorized |
| 403 | Forbidden |
| 404 | Not Found |
